# router_fam_lead.py - router_fam_keys.py plus a sell-advance rim (2026-09-01).
#
# WHY. On 2026-09-01 the field resubmitted en masse and our two active
# submissions collapsed: 55916283 went 4-30 over its last 30 rated episodes,
# losing by a few hundred dollars out of ~100,000. Replays of 24 of those games
# show 11 opponents running OUR farm schedule action-for-action (agreement
# 0.98-1.00 through step 400) with one difference: they place the same SELL
# orders 1-3 hours EARLIER (114 of ~2,300 orders one step early, 48 two, 16
# three, a handful up to six). In a mirror match the first seller takes the
# pre-order price and the second sells into the crash, so a one-hour lead is
# the whole margin - and the ladder pays for the win, not the margin.
#
# WHAT. At step >= 144, look LEAD_K steps ahead in the currently selected
# tape; any SELL of a non-WHEAT/FERTILIZER product whose quantity the shed
# already holds is placed now and skipped at its original step. Quantities
# are unchanged (verified: identical per-product season totals), only timing.
# WHEAT and FERTILIZER stay on schedule because the tape feeds and
# fertilizes from them.
#
# MEASURED (seeds 200-215 both seats unless noted, fam/run_agents.py):
#   mirror vs router_fam_keys.py:   K=1 32-0 +1,907   K=3 32-0 +2,213
#                                   K=6 32-0 +1,854   K=12 32-0 +1,051
#   vs the 9 recorded front-runners (their tapes, seeds 200-207):
#                                   base 64-80   K=1 84-58   K=6 144-0
#   K=6 is the smallest lead that beats every observed opponent lead;
#   K=12 already pays for the extra hours in recovery time.
# Panel of 8 drawn-opponent tapes: see docs/ROUTE_GENERATIONS.md.
#
# SIZE IT HONESTLY: mirrors are ~11 of 24 current draws and we were losing
# ~10 of them. Flipping them returns us to roughly where the lineage sat
# before the wave (rank ~20), it is not the lever to #1.
#
# Key router: our own family's per-shop-draw branches added to router_fam_yarn.
#
# WHAT CHANGED from agents/router_fam_yarn.py (submission 55908478, rank 18 at
# 2,732). Nothing about the opening, and nothing about the YARN_STORE-first
# handover, both of which are left exactly as they are. Six route keys that
# previously fell through to the base schedule now play a recorded branch of
# THE SAME family, chosen at step 144 once both shops are known.
#
# PROVENANCE - eight tapes, all from public ladder replays, all from teams that
# run our own schedule (they share our opening 0.88-1.00 over turns 0-71, which
# is why they can be entered at a branch point at all):
#
#     BAKERY__ICE_CREAM_SHOP        ep 104326196 seat 1  islet (#4)    57,823 vs 54,879
#     FARMERS_MARKET__PIZZA_SHOP    ep 104250455 seat 0  islet (#4)    60,642 vs 60,860
#     FARMERS_MARKET__YARN_STORE    ep 104330775 seat 0  xi luo (#16)  79,086 vs 75,021
#     ICE_CREAM_SHOP__YARN_STORE    ep 104295010 seat 0  xi luo (#16) 131,568 vs 107,397
#     PIZZA_SHOP__PET_CAFE          ep 104315118 seat 0  gogogo (#11)  54,310 vs 52,921
#     PIZZA_SHOP__YARN_STORE        ep 104341845 seat 0  islet (#4)    95,775 vs 77,409
#     YARN_STORE__PET_CAFE          ep 104283848 seat 0  islet (#4)    80,356 vs 81,970
#     YARN_STORE__YARN_STORE        ep 104308288 seat 0  xi luo (#16) 124,752 vs 112,276
#
# The base schedule and the ten YARN_STORE tapes are unchanged from
# agents/router_fam_yarn.py; see that file for the full attribution, including
# the Apache 2.0 notice for yhay81's router, whose tapes and route tables are
# embedded here unmodified. CHANGES BY WASHAMBA BOTS: the eight branches above,
# and the step-144 lookup that selects them.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-01, both seats, contested market, WIN COUNT first - and note
# that win count is the right metric here, not mean bank: on 135 of our own
# rated ladder episodes in steady state, corr(rating change, margin) = +0.002,
# a win is worth +23.6 rating and a loss -11.8 regardless of size. See
# docs/ROUTE_GENERATIONS.md.
#
#   vs agents/router_fam_yarn.py, fresh seeds 240-399, both seats (320 games):
#       46-20 on decided games (254 exact ties - the two agents are the same
#       program on every seed whose route key is not one of the six)
#       worst single game -6,579; min bank identical to the base
#
#   vs a ten-opponent panel (eight tapes of opponents our submission actually
#   drew on the ladder, rated 583-2,529, plus kaito v48 and indarkarhana),
#   seeds 200-215, both seats, 320 games each:
#       this file                   280-40   (87.5%)
#       agents/router_fam_yarn.py   278-42   (86.9%)
#       Semyon Epanov's schedule    262-58   (81.9%)   <- rejected, see below
#
# The margin over the base is +2 games in 320 - inside noise on its own. It
# ships because it is weakly dominant rather than because it is a measured
# gain: it is the base agent on ~80% of draws by construction, it wins more
# than it loses on the rest, and the slot it takes was otherwise holding a
# near-duplicate of the base.
#
# REJECTED on the same evidence, recorded here so it is not retried: the
# Semyon Epanov (#20) and cygn (#14) schedules - single fixed tapes with no
# routing - beat this lineage head to head 54-10 and 52-12 of 64 on fresh
# seeds, and lose to the panel above (81.9% against our 86.9%). They counter
# our schedule specifically and are weaker against the field the ladder
# actually deals. Head-to-head alone would have shipped a regression.

